### Preflight Checklist

- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.
- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.
- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.

### Electron Version

40.1.0

### What operating system(s) are you using?

macOS

### Operating System Version

macOS Sequoia 15.2

### What arch are you using?

arm64 (including Apple Silicon)

### Last Known Working Electron version

~~35.1.2~~ [v39.0.0-beta.3](https://github.com/electron/electron/compare/v39.0.0-beta.3...v39.0.0-beta.4)

### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?

No

### Expected Behavior

Previously, I had used a 0px by 0px screen-capture to achieve Desktop Audio Capture on MacOS with electron. This was a two-step process (code below). 

I expected this working code to continue working on upgrade from `electron 35.1.2 > 40.1.0`

<details>
<summary>Step 1: [NodeJS Init]</summary>

```js
app.whenReady().then( async () => {
//...
  session.defaultSession.setDisplayMediaRequestHandler((request, callback) => {
    desktopCapturer.getSources({ types: ['screen'] }).then((sources) => {
      // Grant access to the first screen found.
      callback({ video: sources[0], audio: 'loopback' })
    })
  })
//...
}
```

</details>

<details>
<summary>Step 2: [ClientSide Access]</summary>

```js
//...
  this.tryScreenAudio=()=>{
    navigator.mediaDevices.getDisplayMedia({
      audio: true,
      video: {
        width: 0,
        height: 0,
        frameRate: 1
      }
    }).then(function(stream) {
	let music = this.context.createMediaStreamSource(stream);
	if(this.inputNode){this.inputNode.disconnect(this.anal)}
	music.connect(this.anal)
	this.inputNode=music;
	this.inputDevice = "DESKTOP AUDIO";
    }.bind(this))
  }
//...
```

</details>

### Actual Behavior

## Major Bug
I can still get a desktop-capture stream after upgrade to 40.1.0. However the stream does not capture audio anymore and instead contains an audio-stream of silence. No errors are omitted, the stream can be confirmed to be playing, the audio analyzer node shows silence.

Since my app is an electron based three.js [music-visualizer](https://soundsafari.io), this is a critical issue for my business.

### Tangential New Issue

Upon update got an error in NodeJS world: `[9982:0130/175946.872027:ERROR:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/video_capture/video_capture_impl.cc:598] Can't wrap SharedImage as VideoFrame`. It seems we can no-longer start a 0px by 0px video stream. It'd be perhaps nice if there was some escape hatch to not immediately wrap a video stream as GPU texture to avoid this error?

This error has a pretty easy work-around, was able to simply do a 4px X 4px capture and all errors vanished:

<details>
<summary>Workaround Configuration</summary>

```js
//...
  navigator.mediaDevices.getDisplayMedia({
    audio: true,
    video: {
      width: 4,
      height: 4,
      frameRate: 1
    }
  })
//...
```

</details>

### Testcase Gist URL

https://gist.github.com/0abf89274d749b1da0ee8f96aafca67a

### Additional Information

Linked is a gist which demonstrates the issue:
1. The nodejs setup for a desktop-capture stream.
2. Minimal page to display the frequency bin volumes of an audio analyzer.
3. The clientside setup to start a 4px X 4px Desktop Capture stream. This stream is connected to an audio-analyzer and the page is updated to show frequency bin volume data via basic `requestAnimationFrame` loop.

Conveniently, if you run this fiddle with electron 35.1.2 it works fine and if you run it with electron 40.1.0 you can see the desktop audio stream is broken (insert joke about silent failure). Here is a video where I run the fiddle on both electron versions (YouTube Link b/c vid too large for GitHub embed):
[![Watch the video](https://img.youtube.com/vi/UpxrB7eyEtI/hqdefault.jpg)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UpxrB7eyEtI)

Debug Notes:
- When you run the fiddle, macOS will prompt you to give `desktop video & audio capture permission` to the Electron-Fiddle application. After granting the permissions, it'll prompt you to restart the Electron Fiddle application so the new permissions can take effect. 
- Probably obvious but don't forget to actually have some audio playing during your test. Since it is desktop-capture the audio can be playing from any application.

Relevant `macOS desktop audio` historical note:
- For a long time, desktop-audio capture was not possible on macOS due to OS Limitation. You may encounter outdated sources which erroneously claim this but in macOS 13 Ventura Apple introduced methods to properly capture Desktop Audio (w/o signed kernel extension). Major applications like OBS [also cite](https://obsproject.com/kb/macos-desktop-audio-capture-guide) this introduced capability of being able to achieve desktop audio via desktop capture with macOS 13 Ventura and onward.

Appreciate your consideration and assistance, put a lot of work into serving this information up in a cohesive way and feel free to reach out with questions. I'll continue to add additional information I discover to this issue. Sorry to drop an issue over the weekend!

